Z||000014||Pontiaddict||07-07-2000||06:14 PM||||Arch, if you think Fiero's are hard to work on, try changing the plugs on a LS1 f-body. <P>Take the same F-car, and run it in the rain after burning half the rubber off the tires! <P>The only problem I had with my 84 on ice happened because I was stupid and didn't check the air pressure in the front tires. <P>If you don't try and race it on the ice you should be fine.<P>Just use common sense and you'll have lots of  fun with these cars!||||reg||1
